{"id": "86287", "name": "מטריצה אלמנטרית 3×3: R₂ ← R₂ + a·R₃ (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.5, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Give the elementary matrix which, when multiplied to the left of a 3 by 3 matrix, will replace row 2 by row 2 + {{CT:0}} times row 3.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\textbf{E} = \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-grid\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: each entry in its own box: a number, a fraction (e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">1/2</code>) or an expression (e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(2)</code>).</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> The elementary matrix of a row operation is obtained by performing that operation on the identity matrix.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Apply the row operation to the identity</b><br>If left multiplication by <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(E\\)</span> performs a row operation, then in particular <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(EI=E\\)</span> is the result of that operation on <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(I\\)</span>. So we perform <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(R_2\\leftarrow R_2+{{CT:1}}R_3\\)</span> on the <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(3\\times 3\\)</span> identity matrix.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The elementary matrix</b><br>Row 3 of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(I\\)</span> is <span dir=\"ltr\">\\((0,0,1)\\)</span>. Adding <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:1}}\\)</span> times it to row 2, <span dir=\"ltr\">\\((0,1,0)\\)</span>, gives <span dir=\"ltr\">\\((0,1,{{CT:1}})\\)</span>; the other rows do not change:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\mathbf{E}={{CT:2}} \\]</p>Check: for any <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(3\\times 3\\)</span> matrix <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(M\\)</span>, row 2 of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\mathbf{E}M\\)</span> is <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(1\\cdot R_2+{{CT:1}}\\cdot R_3\\)</span> of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(M\\)</span>, and the other rows are unchanged.</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "matrix", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "determinant, invert", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["avar", "correctanswer", "wronganswer1"], "nvariants": 5}